<title>JAPAN: SHORT TRACK SPEED SKATING-WORLD CHAMPIONSHIP RESULTS.</title>
<headline>SHORT TRACK SPEED SKATING-WORLD CHAMPIONSHIP RESULTS.</headline>
<dateline>NAGANO, Japan 1997-03-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Results on the first day</p>
<p>of the world short track speed skating championships at White</p>
<p>Ring arena on Friday: </p>
<p>Men</p>
<p>1,500 metres</p>
<p>  1. Marc Gagnon (Canada)	    2:21.322</p>
<p>  2. Orazio Fagone (Italy)	   2:21.617</p>
<p>  3. Mirko Vuillermin (Italy)	2:22.063</p>
<p>  4. Feng Kai (China)		  2:22.171</p>
<p>  5. Lee Jun-Hwan (South Korea)    2:22.539</p>
<p>  6. Martin Johansson (Sweden)     2:25.993</p>
<p>Disqualified: Kim Dong-Sung (South Korea)</p>
<p>Women</p>
<p>1,500 metres</p>
<p>1. Chun Lee-Kyung (South Korea)  2:29.426</p>
<p>  2. Won Hye-Kyung (South Korea)   2:29.554</p>
<p>  3. Yang Yang (S) (China)	   2:30.467</p>
<p>  4. Ikue Teshigawara (Japan)	2:32.768</p>
<p>  5. Kim Yun-Mi (South Korea)	2:59.259</p>
<p>Disqualified: Yang Yang (A) (China)</p>
</text>
